    "narrative": "For the May 28th slate, **Zach McKinstry** headlines our daily lineup with a score of 56.30, narrowly edging out **Austin Riley** (56.08) for the top spot. **Zach McKinstry** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.95 xERA suggests a volatile outing ripe for exploitation, allowing our 2B to capitalize on a favorable park factor and a strong surge in recency metrics. While **Austin Riley** faces the lefty Tolle\u2014usually a recipe for a massive ceiling\u2014the moderate xERA of 3.79 tempers his projection slightly, though his reliability in the #5 spot makes him an essential cornerstone of today's scoring core.\n\nThe most difficult decision was managing **Seiya Suzuki**, who barely cleared our marginal threshold at 43.87. Despite the wind blowing out at the park\u2014providing a necessary +5% boost\u2014he faces the daunting challenge of Paul Skenes. With an elite 3.03 xERA, Skenes serves as a primary risk factor that significantly suppressed **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s ceiling; he remains in the lineup only due to a lack of deeper viable alternatives today. Our bench remains stagnant, as players like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** are all sitting on off-days, depriving the roster of our core speed and power density. Looking ahead, we need to ensure that bench depth remains hydrated for when **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, and **Gabriel Moreno** cycle back into active status to chase those high-value SB and HR counts. \n\nManaging the fringes of our prospect stash\u2014including **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Cole Young**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014remains a secondary priority as we monitor their progression against the daily 5x5 requirements. We are strictly adhering to the daily efficiency floor; if any of our starters see their lineup placement move down or weather conditions shift to depress scoring, we will not hesitate to sub to protect our game caps.",
